  "cause": "Sampling origins used the compact ink request instead of the filter destination request. Complete clip coverage can extend beyond its shortened paint window. Nonopaque filters own a painted-output enclosure; an explicit owned destination has already consumed its parent clip. Logical paint-classification bounds are not that destination window.",
  "correction": "Reuse the existing retained-coverage lookup with an explicit search window. Seed generic and offset source-image sampling from complete clip coverage inside the current destination, intersecting the existing painted-output bounds for nonopaque filter restoration. Preserve the earlier ink request for geometry capture and storage. Reuse propagated bounds when requests are equal; share the nonopaque extent with ordinary restoration. No dither phase override is introduced.",
  "ownerDistinctions": {
    "paint": "Raster-frame/scope logical clips still classify geometric/viewport paints independently of compact storage.",
    "sampling": "A current owned destination uses its clipped addressable enclosure for filter output requests; its parent clip has already been consumed. Nonopaque inline filters use the same painted-output enclosure as an explicit surrounding opacity group.",
    "construction": "Conservative source geometry and its allocation continue using the original propagated ink request; unrelated ink is not captured to alter line/curve construction."
  },
